AB  - Its registers for the first time the presence of the African giant snail, Achatina fulica (Bowdich 1822) in Sincelejo city, department of Sucre, Caribbean coast of Colombia. The first invasion alert in the country was given by Corpoamazonia in August of 2010, for introduction of snails coming from Brazil. Then in the year 2011 was reported the occurrence in the departments of Arauca, Boyacá, Caquetá, Casanare, Guainía, Huila, Meta, Nariño, Putumayo, Santander, Tolima, Valle del Cauca and Vaupés. In the 2012 it was located in the department of Antioquia. This new discovery in the department of Sucre alerts because its presence in the Colombian Caribbean begins to be certain.
